#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "aebe3048-cc5b-5340-a15e-d577ae2ee72a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5479" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n![](images/36/36c1ce5342657231cd78154ab4821a6a5bf9b78b74297ae5a4cdccdc2f6d5dcd.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/1c/1cab5be2ed7c560a3a5192473be4ff7b6cf6dc5728552f1d179c73affebefe20.svg)\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-4\\cdot 3 & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/id #uuid "55e695b2-4581-5ba7-9604-506234b88323" :question/math-academy-id "e-5480" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n![](images/2c/2c669dd6f7c5fa368c5ea28961d2ef57cac9deaf7ba453f75a441b05206f6276.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/e4/e4e91261ec7f4a9a48847005a57730afa25f5e69a1f3818ad583acaadae639f8.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(B-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $B$ has only one eigenvalue $\\lambda=4,$ which is a double root of the characteristic equation. \n\n**Note:** We also say that $\\lambda=4$ has an **algebraic multiplicity** of $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "864cf210-cbb0-5a79-b90a-33a5df332559" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With Two Distinct Eigenvalues"}] :question/id #uuid "a42d0af8-869c-5c2a-8182-22b14b9546e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5481" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/9f/9f13c3379e0613ce91669f6e52473dd11dc95360c422943764f30220dbccf430.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿![](images/03/039ee6073538580614cc07453132b811a4da81f438abf37197bb686057b4b66c.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 6 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-3\\cdot 6 & =0 \\\\ 70-7\\lambda -10\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-17\\lambda +52 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{(-17)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 52}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm \\sqrt{81}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pm 9}{2} \\\\  & =13,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda=13$ and $\\lambda=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092077 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "9e40836e-18e9-5df6-a930-05875b920335" :question/math-academy-id "e-5482" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix ![](images/e3/e34b5bf690a1dd8f5275f2d742b264494386b95394bc7c32aaafb9eeba68e058.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $A - \\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/37/37f547d6ad345415a1cc2480adf227ec29e31a351cf935e584b9544e44347310.svg)\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $\\det (A - \\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 9 & -2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2\\sqrt{3}-\\lambda )-9\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2\\sqrt{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the eigenvalues $\\lambda={\\color{red}3}$ and $\\lambda={\\color{blue}-2\\sqrt{3}}.$\n\nIf we look again at the matrix ![](images/f4/f4e86a797cafe4857d5f135ec37d57e33368469767e50793f55b89ec7185c2eb.svg)\nwe see that the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. This is true in general: the eigenvalues of a *triangular* or *diagonal* matrix are *always* given by the entries on the main diagonal!\n\n**Watch out!** For a general matrix (which is neither triangular nor diagonal), this might not be the case!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a787981-8115-531c-a0b2-45614b628dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446651} {:answer/id #uuid "514631b5-18c9-56ed-b862-2cfc925d4f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446655} {:answer/id #uuid "d0015afe-6401-5c12-9cf2-8b51092f7180" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446699} {:answer/id #uuid "e79a4073-0867-556b-8d5c-c5025c11ea29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446703} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd3bb9f-f42f-5091-bf4d-48c5dff63db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a787981-8115-531c-a0b2-45614b628dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446651} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9ffc0b3-2fb7-50ab-863d-ef122a417f29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2d1ce53-250c-556e-b39c-e7210e507a13" :question/math-academy-id "q-106947" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 9 & =0 \\\\ -12-4\\lambda +3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -30 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092229 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbf5fbb2-688a-5833-87b9-37229c8fb692" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be045a5-6b6f-58a1-a9c0-054dd780305c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446652} {:answer/id #uuid "680fa24a-7dc3-543d-85de-5db5562557f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446660} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3e29e7-ff34-52ad-a2b3-30b0d4dfc7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446683} {:answer/id #uuid "bb76f2d9-d38e-5ad5-b5ba-f0c456c42a65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda +8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446689} {:answer/id #uuid "ee278763-ab63-504f-822f-61b01cf166d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3be045a5-6b6f-58a1-a9c0-054dd780305c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446652} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ff74171-fb77-58e8-9b4d-b1ac71573691" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a11188a-8a0f-5ab5-9de2-8d85b1d9c9bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-106954" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-2) & =0 \\\\ 4-\\lambda -4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092230 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d235bca-d848-5075-affb-09e3103cfc11" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Eigenvalues of a Matrix With At Most One Distinct Eigenvalue"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "731c273b-83ef-5ecf-bca7-30fd9429facb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446666} {:answer/id #uuid "75cd4420-20f3-5ded-8c44-39d55a82ae27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-6$ and $\\lambda =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446668} {:answer/id #uuid "77ff9bd5-364c-5949-a133-ce7f4bb78ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446670} {:answer/id #uuid "9c38e99e-6b40-58d6-baca-ae8ea0b40eb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =1$ and $\\lambda =6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446684} {:answer/id #uuid "cecd0803-36c1-5916-aeae-507fa6a5a5c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cecd0803-36c1-5916-aeae-507fa6a5a5c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446698} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4615f19-9c7a-5091-99a4-538030c0787d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "86473df3-55aa-5a6b-9f10-9b94fded00fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-106988" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$Q=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -9 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $Q-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nQ-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & -9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(Q-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & -9 \\\\ 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )-2\\cdot (-9) & =0 \\\\ -12-4\\lambda +3\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+18 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-1)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =1-24 \\\\  & =-23 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $Q$ does not have real eigenvalues."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446734 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a3c3fb8-6cb0-50c4-9ef3-126838f4ce82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446646} {:answer/id #uuid "57e4e92d-8154-5972-94f3-6a2be941a297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446656} {:answer/id #uuid "8688b5da-0cea-5d1e-9ba0-2678fa02cf28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =7$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446674} {:answer/id #uuid "aa4c8e25-fb81-5e27-b673-2b99b02a167e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446686} {:answer/id #uuid "ed046ba9-c6f5-5ba6-8016-8beac476dce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57e4e92d-8154-5972-94f3-6a2be941a297" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-2$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446656} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc20a709-7b8c-57c3-b33e-d46ed2185a69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446729}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f368600-216e-5acd-8869-df093ce09e0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-106996" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(C-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =7$ and $\\lambda =-2.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446743 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b663abe-8ca9-5e98-a421-8ee08f7f4b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446657} {:answer/id #uuid "602aa1ad-6d56-50d3-a5b0-1aeda4a4c661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =18$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446659} {:answer/id #uuid "80774a76-6156-58a8-a1af-8130684f2c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =6$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446671} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfa7309-3f10-57c3-852d-7167399f1f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-18$ and $\\lambda =6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446678} {:answer/id #uuid "f47791cc-1060-50da-baa1-ca82124c18ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =6$ and $\\lambda =18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8dfa7309-3f10-57c3-852d-7167399f1f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-18$ and $\\lambda =6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446678} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d8c02f9-48d0-57c8-9419-e72e043a5824" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0119bb7-296f-5cbc-ac52-c9d22940b932" :question/math-academy-id "q-107001" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(C-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & -18-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )(-18-\\lambda )-0\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +18) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-18$ and $\\lambda =6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446745 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd4158d-6baf-5a61-96a2-74c66231d082" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a Triangular/Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b5bb84-0f48-5dfe-81a5-5623dd7f6712" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446633} {:answer/id #uuid "0d6e90a2-f4f0-5b73-a742-96283d76f4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446636} {:answer/id #uuid "600134d3-9568-5f5f-8691-d69f8a228619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\lambda =-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446658} {:answer/id #uuid "ce79e6ac-6a71-5954-97e0-e2449988d58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446697} {:answer/id #uuid "e1884e2a-420c-50b7-a538-8daff46abc19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident 